* SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-S-2.0
* Architecture model, NOT a transistor/macromodel of the named BOM parts.
* Engineering assumptions: 4.5 m, 5.05 ns/m, 1 ohm/conductor total,
* 5 pF shunt at each cable terminal, finite differential output impedance.
.subckt cable p n q r
Rlp p pt 0.5
Rln n nt 0.5
Tp pt 0 qt 0 Z0=55 TD=22.725n
Tn nt 0 rt 0 Z0=55 TD=22.725n
Rrp qt q 0.5
Rrn rt r 0.5
Clp p 0 5p
Cln n 0 5p
Crp q 0 5p
Crn r 0 5p
.ends cable

* Signed cmd -1/0/1 selects zero/Z/one; differential branch has ZERO net CM.
* cm current is explicitly separate, allowing source/sink mismatch/skew tests.
* Analog rail headroom not qualified: model smoothly rolls current off beyond
* 0.2..2.8 V common-mode, rather than pretending unlimited voltage compliance.
.subckt driver p n cmd cm params: amp=4m mismatch=0 leak=0
Bsig n p I={amp*v(cmd)*min(1,max(0,((v(p)+v(n))/2-0.2)/0.2))*min(1,max(0,(2.8-(v(p)+v(n))/2)/0.2))}
BcmP 0 p I={v(cm)/2 + mismatch*abs(v(cmd))/2 - leak/2}
BcmN 0 n I={v(cm)/2 + mismatch*abs(v(cmd))/2 - leak/2}
Rout p n 100k
.ends driver

* Local A to remote B. Receiver loading is in cable endpoint 5p assumption.
* TPBIAS source impedance is an assumption; opamp stability is NOT modeled.
.subckt port_pair p n q r vref lc rc lcm rcm params: ampL=4m ampR=4m mis=0
Xwire p n q r cable
Rpa p ct 55
Rna n ct 55
Rbias vref ct 5
Cbias ct 0 1u
Rpb q ctr 55
Rnb r ctr 55
Rbleed ctr 0 5k
Cbleed ctr 0 220p
Xl p n lc lcm driver amp={ampL} mismatch={mis}
Xr q r rc rcm driver amp={ampR} mismatch={mis}
.ends port_pair

* High-impedance arbitration path. 10 MHz SINGLE POLE is an assumption inspired
* by AD8421 G=1 bandwidth, NOT its vendor model or settling guarantee.
.subckt window p n pos neg
Rinp p 0 30g
Rinn n 0 30g
Bdiff raw 0 V={v(p,n)}
Rbw raw filtered 1k
Cbw filtered 0 15.915p
Bpos pos 0 V={v(filtered)>0.125 ? 1 : 0}
Bneg neg 0 V={v(filtered)<-0.125 ? 1 : 0}
.ends window
